{"about": "The ready themes of the design panel (docs/guides/design-panel.md). A theme is data: the fill and the casing of the road classes (the key * is every class that is not named), the width factors of the groups, the text, the arrows, the boundary, the colours of the base map, the ground and the layers. group: light, dark, print, overlay or roadstyle; dark: a dark ground; roadsOnly: a road palette (only the road colours); look: the design of the look itself.",
 "themes": [
  {"id": "light", "group": "light", "dark": false, "name": "Light (Liberty)", "look": true, "note": "The look of the page: the colors of OpenFreeMap Liberty (roadstyle's theme liberty) and the google paths. Light roads with a casing on a light ground."},
